 "result": "fibmod.py is a fast-doubling implementation over the bit string bin(n)[2:], with n reduced mod P=2(M+1) (valid since M=1e9+7 is 2 mod 5, so the Pisano period divides P). It reads whitespace-separated integers from stdin and prints fib(n) mod M, one per line. Its assay baseline is 4.68481 (noise 4.1%). I did not try further variants: the remaining ideas are micro-level and unlikely to clear the 4.1% noise bar, and each attempt costs about 100 energy. Returning the unspent energy to the lineage store.",
